{#- F-258 fresh-standup bootstrap of the portal-owned ORG FRAGMENT (per-vendor
    mode only). Reproduces, BYTE-IDENTICALLY, the seed-vendor content that used
    to render inline between the per-vendor markers in config.json5.j2, under the
    ##ACL-ORG-REGION headers acl-assemble.py splices back. Rendered ONCE by the
    role when no fragment exists yet; a re-render never overwrites a fragment
    that already holds vendors (acl-assemble init-org / the role guard). The
    storages section is intentionally empty: seed-vendor storages render in the
    seed ABOVE the markers (config.json5.j2), so they are role-owned, not here.
    The write-rules comment + the three loops are copied verbatim from the old
    config.json5.j2 render — see the byte-faithfulness test in tests/. -#}
##ACL-ORG-REGION storages
##ACL-ORG-REGION write-rules
      // INGRESS-only after the ADR 1020 split — this is the ONLY thing
      // that lets a vendor PUBLISH, and only into its own namespace.
      // Egress delivery is universal via trial-peer-deliver-all.
      //
      // One grant per peer, two prefixes (ADR 1032): the persisted
      // <vendor>/** namespace + the non-persisted volatile/<vendor>/**
      // class. Same identity boundary; volatile/<vendor>/** has NO
      // storage entry (so nothing reaches rocksdb) and is excluded by the
      // audit subscriber (--exclude-key volatile/**), so it routes live
      // but is never persisted. Granting this write WITHOUT the audit
      // exclude active would route the firehose into the locked audit
      // bucket — keep them in lockstep.
{% for vendor in zenoh_seed_vendors %}
      {
        id: "trial-peer-w-{{ vendor }}",
        messages: ["put", "delete", "liveliness_token"],
        flows: ["ingress"],
        permission: "allow",
        key_exprs: ["{{ vendor }}/**", "volatile/{{ vendor }}/**", "{{ vendor }}/**/@adv/**"],
      },
{% endfor %}
##ACL-ORG-REGION subjects
{% for vendor in zenoh_seed_vendors %}
      {
        id: "vendor-{{ vendor }}",
        cert_common_names: ["{{ vendor }}-trial-peer"],
      },
{% endfor %}
##ACL-ORG-REGION policies
{% for vendor in zenoh_seed_vendors %}
      {
        rules: ["trial-peer-w-{{ vendor }}", "trial-peer-w-attest-schema"],
        subjects: ["vendor-{{ vendor }}"],
      },
{% endfor %}
